{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01F5GuJyoTXAdZJpeHAjU8ZV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully to understand what needs to be done.\n\n## Project Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. It's an experiment in specification-driven development.\n\n**Architecture**: \n- `cmd/<name>/` - One utility per directory\n- `pkg/testutils/` - Differential testing framework\n- `pkg/sys/` - System calls\n- `pkg/format/` - Output formatting\n- `pkg/hashutil/` - Hash utilities (shared by checksum commands)\n\n\n- `pkg/sizeparse/` - Size parsing\n- `pkg/encutil/` - Encoding utilities\n- `docs/specs/` - SRDs, use cases, test suites\n- `magefiles/` - Build automation\n\n**Current State**: Most utilities haven't been started yet, with only a few packages already implemented: the system calls wrapper, hash utilities, size parsing, and encoding utilities. Everything else is waiting to be built.\n\n**Requirement States**: All requirements across the SRDs are marked ready, so nothing's been completed or is actively in progress.\n\n**Package Contracts**: I have the contracts for testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, and encutil already defined, and four of these packages are already implemented.\n\n**Release Priority**: Release 00.0 is the first incomplete release. It needs magefiles, format utilities, and testutils to be built, while the system calls, hash utilities, and size parsing are already done.\n\nNow I'm checking the magefiles requirements more carefully. The architecture says magefiles is external infrastructure, so the only generation target should be cmd/version. Looking at the requirement states for srd011-magefiles, only R5.1 is marked ready, but I see from recent commits that the cmd/version binary was already completed. I need to figure out